{"name":"Great Falls","hex":"#9fa6b3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Great Falls","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of waterfalls in North America.","A city, the county seat of Cascade County, Montana, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Great_Falls"}],"entries":[{"title":"Great Falls, Montana","blocks":[{"text":"Great Falls is the third most populous city in the U.S. state of Montana and the county seat of Cascade County. The population was 60,442 according to the 2020 census. The city covers an area of 22.9 square miles (59 km2) and is the principal city of the Great Falls, Montana, Metropolitan Statistical Area, which encompasses all of Cascade County. The Great Falls MSA's population was 84,414 according to the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Central_Ave_and_Civic_Center_2.JPG/330px-Central_Ave_and_Civic_Center_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Falls%2C_Montana"},{"title":"Great Falls (Passaic River)","blocks":[{"text":"The Great Falls of the Passaic River is a 77-foot-high (23 m) waterfall on the Passaic River in the city of Paterson in Passaic County, New Jersey. One of the United States' largest waterfalls, it played a significant role in the early industrial development of New Jersey starting in the earliest days of the nation. The falls and surrounding area are protected as part of the Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park, administered by the National Park Service. Congress authorized its establishment in 2009."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Great_Falls_of_Paterson_2016.jpg/330px-Great_Falls_of_Paterson_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Falls_(Passaic_River)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik